\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Downside-risk behavior of $C_2$ and $C_3^{\mathrm  R}$ across syndrome regimes. Panel~(a) shows the false-safe fidelity rate $\mathrm  {FS}_F$. Panel~(b) shows the lower-tail fidelity-gain $\mathrm  {CVaR}_{0.05}$. The robust controller is inactive in clean and noisy-only controls, but reduces false-safe fidelity failures and improves lower-tail CVaR in partial and partial-plus-noisy regimes. The ambiguity-plus-measurement regime, hatched on the right, is included as a secondary stress control.}}{12}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c3r-downside-risk}{{2}{12}{Downside-risk behavior of $C_2$ and $C_3^{\mathrm R}$ across syndrome regimes. Panel~(a) shows the false-safe fidelity rate $\mathrm {FS}_F$. Panel~(b) shows the lower-tail fidelity-gain $\mathrm {CVaR}_{0.05}$. The robust controller is inactive in clean and noisy-only controls, but reduces false-safe fidelity failures and improves lower-tail CVaR in partial and partial-plus-noisy regimes. The ambiguity-plus-measurement regime, hatched on the right, is included as a secondary stress control}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Intervention quality of $C_3^{\mathrm  R}$ in regimes where it actively blocks $C_2$ switches. Panel~(a) reports the conditional intervention rates: block rate (given $C_2=B$), harmful-block precision, harmful-switch recall, and beneficial-switch block rate. Panel~(b) shows the aggregate intervention balance, comparing prevented harmful-switch loss, missed beneficial-switch gain, and the resulting net effect, all in fidelity-gain units. Panel~(c) normalizes the net effect per blocked switch and per $C_2$-proposed switch to separate aggregate benefit from the number of vetoed proposals. The ambiguity-plus-measurement regime is hatched as a secondary stress control.}}{12}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c3r-intervention-quality}{{3}{12}{Intervention quality of $C_3^{\mathrm R}$ in regimes where it actively blocks $C_2$ switches. Panel~(a) reports the conditional intervention rates: block rate (given $C_2=B$), harmful-block precision, harmful-switch recall, and beneficial-switch block rate. Panel~(b) shows the aggregate intervention balance, comparing prevented harmful-switch loss, missed beneficial-switch gain, and the resulting net effect, all in fidelity-gain units. Panel~(c) normalizes the net effect per blocked switch and per $C_2$-proposed switch to separate aggregate benefit from the number of vetoed proposals. The ambiguity-plus-measurement regime is hatched as a secondary stress control}{figure.3}{}}
